{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon","id":46292,"title":"What about Gods who are worshipped in more than one Pantheon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T08:57:08-08:00","id":46292,"title":"What about Gods who are worshipped in more than one Pantheon?","content":"It's well-known that the Theoi have both their Greek and Roman personas and that their personalities and identities change a bit in their Greek and Roman aspects. At least some of them do. Ares is more the &quot;noble warrior&quot; kinda guy when he's Mars, for example.<br /> <br /> Guan Yin is worshipped both in China and Japan and, I believe, she's even revered in Hinduism. She's considered a member of both the Shen, the Kami, and she may even be welcome among the Devas.<br /> <br /> Mithra is a member of the Yazatas, and yet he was also worshipped by the Romans (Theoi) and even the Hindus (Devas).<br /> <br /> Isis was widely worshipped throughout the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> There may be others that I'm just not thinking about right now, but that's enough examples for what I'm asking.<br /> <br /> How does Scion handle these Gods who technically belong to more than one Pantheon? Do they have a whole separate identity within each Pantheon? Or are they pretty much their &quot;default&quot; persona and just happen to be welcome amongst the Gods of their other Pantheons?<br /> <br /> Perhaps more importantly? Okay, the general rule is that Gods only get one PSP, but for a God who is considered a member of another Pantheon, can they somehow switch? I mean, Guan Yin is worshipped just as seriously in Shintoism as she is among the Shen. Does she have Taiyi, or Tsukumo-Gami? Or can she perhaps switch between those by switching between her Chinese and Japanese identities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T09:35:06-08:00","id":46313,"title":"","content":"The Gods you describe can be safely put into a number of categories and then dealt with appropriately.<br /> <br /> First, the easiest. Isis might have been widely worshipped in the Roman Empire, but she was worshipped as an Egyptian Goddess. No one tried to pass her off as a Roman deity, as far as I know. Thus, this case is not a case at all. Isis remains Egyptian and retains only Heku.<br /> <br /> Second, Gods like Mithra, who <i>are</i> worshipped in more than one Pantheon, but whose importance in one vastly outshines their importance in the other. Mithra is amongst the most important of the Yazata, but a Deva so unimportant that his very name is now better remembered as an appellation of Surya than a God unto himself. Mithra should therefore be a Yazata, and have Asha.<br /> <br /> Third, we have the eternally confusing Greco-Roman Pantheon. How this situation is treated depends massively on ST decisions and personal settings. If, in your settings, the Greek and Roman Pantheons are just one Pantheon, then no question arises. If, on the other hand, they are different, then two things can be done. Firstly, you may hold that Mars and Ares are two different Gods altogether, and give them their respective PSPs. Or, you may assume that the uniquely Roman Gods, like Janus or Pomona, are a Pantheon as a whole subservient to the Greek Pantheon. In this case, Ares/Mars should only have Arete. He is a Greek God being worshipped by the Romans, and his personality differences can be put down to personal quirks. Also, note that the portrayal of Mars is, obviously, more recent than that of Ares. His more mature personality can be put down to his having grown up from his Greek days.<br /> <br /> Finally, we have the actual problem children. The rare few Gods like Guan Yin and Quetzalcoatl who are honestly and widely worshipped as members of multiple Pantheons. I would put it down to ST choice. But I would say the best answer is: <b>follow the mythology, not the religion</b>. Guan Yin is widely worshipped across the Far East, but her most specific myths all occur in China, like her interaction with the Monkey King and the children of the Dragon King. Kukulkan was undoubtedly an important God for the Maya, but we have more mythology for Quetzalcoatl. Thus, they would be Shen and Teotl respectively.<br /> <br /> Hope that helped. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-10-2014, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T09:38:51-08:00","id":46316,"title":"","content":"This is a messy issue because it happens <i>a lot. </i>Pretty much any time cultures mesh, they'll appropriate each other's religions to some degree. With PC's, it's fairly simple. They started out as members of one Pantheon and then, later, acquired worshippers or Fatebonds that tied them to another Pantheon. You always know a PC's original Pantheon. No questions.<br /> <br /> It's much harder for existing Gods, because their origins aren't always clear. Some are! Epona started out Gaulish and was adopted by Rome. The Romans adopted a <i>lot</i> of Gods. They adopted Isis and Mithras. In cases like that, it's easy to say that they're still Gaulish, Egyptian and Persian, but they've developed cults and ties to the Roman Pantheon. It's harder with gods like Quetzalcoatl, who isn't <i>quite</i> the same as Kukulkan. Is he the same God with different names, or two different Gods that are just very much alike? <br /> <br /> <br /> I would run it individually in each case. It also depends on if you plan on your chronicle ever reaching God-level. If not, what does it matter if some Gods are able to be in multiple Pantheons and, thus, can wield different PSPs when in their different forms? Maybe when she's in Chinese territory, Guan Yin has Taiyi, but if she crosses into Shinto territory, she loses it and gains Tsukumo-Gami. That becomes problematic with PC's at God-level, since you have to run things for Gods according to the same rules that will be used for PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T12:07:15-08:00","id":46396,"title":"","content":"Nothing in Scion says people cannot worship -- and more importantly, tell stories about -- another culture's Gods. What's more, nothing in Scion says that Gods could not interact with Gods of other pantheons before the present day. So if there's a &quot;problem&quot; with Gods appearing in multiple cultural contexts and mythologies, it's a problem of us being neat-freaks and trying to place everything in tidy boxes, rather than a problem with the setting. <br /> <br /> I'd nominate Coyote as a prime example. Numerous Native American cultures told stories about Coyote. He even appears in lists of Aztec Gods. This does not mean Coyote has to be Atzlanti, or that there have to be multiple Coyotes. It just means that mortals really really liked stories about his highjinks, so those stories spread. And maybe the stories spread so much because Coyote got around and interacted with mortals of several cultures, and with their Gods. <br /> <br /> (I have no idea which Native American culture Coyote is most associated with, whose pantheon would be his pantheon of origin. It might not even be possible to discover, making Coyote's assignment to any particular pantheon rather arbitrary. So it goes when you try to fit messy reality into game categories.) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T12:20:05-08:00","id":46401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=46396#post46396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in Scion says people cannot worship -- and more importantly, tell stories about -- another culture's Gods. What's more, nothing in Scion says that Gods could not interact with Gods of other pantheons before the present day. So if there's a &quot;problem&quot; with Gods appearing in multiple cultural contexts and mythologies, it's a problem of us being neat-freaks and trying to place everything in tidy boxes, rather than a problem with the setting.<br /> <br /> I'd nominate Coyote as a prime example. Numerous Native American cultures told stories about Coyote. He even appears in lists of Aztec Gods. This does not mean Coyote has to be Atzlanti, or that there have to be multiple Coyotes. It just means that mortals really really liked stories about his highjinks, so those stories spread. And maybe the stories spread so much because Coyote got around and interacted with mortals of several cultures, and with their Gods.<br /> <br /> (I have no idea which Native American culture Coyote is most associated with, whose pantheon would be his pantheon of origin. It might not even be possible to discover, making Coyote's assignment to any particular pantheon rather arbitrary. So it goes when you try to fit messy reality into game categories.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with the general point of your post, I will say, as far as I know, that Coyote isn't a very good example. There isn't one Coyote running around North America being all trickster like. There are, in fact, multiple trickster Coyote Gods in different Pantheons with certain overarching traits. It's not dissimilar to how multiple Eurasian Pantheons have hot-headed thunder gods who can't keep it in their pants and (usually) have a love of drinking. The many Coyote Gods are no more the same person than Zeus, Thor, Indra and Perun are the same person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T12:52:28-08:00","id":46437,"title":"","content":"I think Coyote is perhaps the one personage that's very unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T13:19:19-08:00","id":46456,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/12/cunning-canine-corporation.html\" target=\"_blank\">For an enjoyable read on the <i>many, many</i> &quot;Coyotes&quot;. </a><br /> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/11/bird-is-word.html\" target=\"_blank\">She did one on &quot;Raven&quot;, too. </a><br /> <br /> Samudra is correct, Europeans simply translated, literally, the names of various Gods from different religions and mushed them together. It really would be like saying every European Thunder God is the same person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T13:33:37-08:00","id":46462,"title":"","content":"From a proto-European point of view, the one Thunder God might be true. Of course, separate entities do evolve over time...soo...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T13:55:13-08:00","id":46471,"title":"","content":"You're correct, it is in fact possible that at one point in pre-history, the humans entering that continent for the first time only had one Thunder God and that concept evolved divergently as that group of humans differentiated and moved into separate locations.<br /> <br /> However, trying to reconcile historical anthropology and Scion is a struggle that leads down the murky, and boring, road of monomythology. All War Gods are really just aspects of the platonic IDEAL of a &quot;War God&quot;.. blah. Boring. LAME.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T15:04:55-08:00","id":46525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=46396#post46396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I have no idea which Native American culture Coyote is most associated with, whose pantheon would be his pantheon of origin. It might not even be possible to discover, making Coyote's assignment to any particular pantheon rather arbitrary. So it goes when you try to fit messy reality into game categories.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most&quot; is impossible to quantify. He's a totem spirit for pretty much every Native American culture present west of the Appalachians and south of Puget Sound prior to the removal of Natives from their ancestral homes. The North and Eastern tribes probably didn't see many actual coyotes since they were in wolf ranges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T15:26:16-08:00","id":46538,"title":"","content":"Another possibility to consider would be to allow a god to \u201cswitch allegiances\u201d, forsaking his original Pantheon\u2019s PSP and adopting a different one. Note that helping establish a new Pantheon would be a special case of this. Put another way, don\u2019t treat the Pantheons as something that\u2019s static; treat them as something dynamic that have changed over the ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T22:53:16-08:00","id":46760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=46471#post46471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're correct, it is in fact possible that at one point in pre-history, the humans entering that continent for the first time only had one Thunder God and that concept evolved divergently as that group of humans differentiated and moved into separate locations.<br /> <br /> However, trying to reconcile historical anthropology and Scion is a struggle that leads down the murky, and boring, road of monomythology. All War Gods are really just aspects of the platonic IDEAL of a &quot;War God&quot;.. blah. Boring. LAME.</div> </div> </div> </div>as a polytheist, I also reject it. The various gods and goddesses are all unique; unless it is clear that the other name was one of their guises or alises; ie Wotan and Odin. I think part of this issue is yet another Monotheistic baggage that we have. what baggage is this?<br /> <br /> A clear cut boxing in of the gods and goddesses. There -<u><i><b>Never</b></i></u>- was a clear cut definition as to what was part of the pantheons. The gauls near the german area, worshiped some gaulish deities and some german ones as their own. Romans did the same. Hell, there was not one Gaelic, Germanic, Greek, or so on religion but religions. <br /> <br /> now, I am not saying that the concept of a pantheon, was a monotheistic concept; it was not. The romans built the pantheon for all of their major gods after all. But the exclusivity part, is something that is monotheistic. Sorry for the little rant btw. <br /> <br /> As for Scion, I would do it this way, what ever branch of myths she/he focuses on the most, say Gaelic, Jappanese, Chinese, or so on. It just happens that people worship from a different panthon, which is -<u><i><b>normal</b></i></u>-, If there are two branches of stories. Say chinese and japanese, then they are the same deity with different stories. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T23:01:13-08:00","id":46762,"title":"","content":"An example that I can think of is when the Greeks learned of the Egyptian pantheon of deities. To explain, they claimed that during the early stages of the war against the Titans, Zeus and the other gods and goddesses escaped to Egypt, where they were worshipped under Egyptian names. There was mention in the Kane Chronicles that Thoth was angry at Hermes because the Greeks attributed him to the Greek messenger god, which he thought was an insult to his character.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a god of multiple pantheons seems to be a cop-out for anyone to explain within their reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T06:49:09-08:00","id":46868,"title":"","content":"Being in multiple pantheons sounds like they'd have more work to do in order to preserve their integrity. Appearing in numerous cultures' myths means you are now subject to numerous cultures' fatebonds at the same time. You could wake up not knowing who you are from the flood of alternate perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T11:10:46-08:00","id":46980,"title":"","content":"Since the page Telgar cites won't open for me, I'll take your word for it. But I think the point stands that the &quot;problem&quot; lies in the assumption that mythologies and pantheons must be completely sealed from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T14:33:14-08:00","id":47075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon#post46292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guan Yin is worshipped both in China and Japan and, I believe, she's even revered in Hinduism. She's considered a member of both the Shen, the Kami, and she may even be welcome among the Devas.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's a bodhisattva, so my prefernce would be to place her in a Buddhist pantheon, perhaps with honorary status in the Celestial Bureaucracy/Amatsukami. This suits the syncretic tendencies of East Asian religion, or at least Buddhism and various local mythologie<b>s.</b><br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think about it, Guan Yin should probably remain a Shen, with status among the Kami and a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avalokite%C5%9Bvara\" target=\"_blank\">masculine alter ago</a> in the hypothetical Buddhist pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 01-11-2014, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T07:55:30-08:00","id":47382,"title":"","content":"Whats about the Gods who originated through cultural mixing , like Serapis ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:59:52-08:00","id":47482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=47382#post47382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats about the Gods who originated through cultural mixing , like Serapis ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be not real, a guise of one of the originals, a guise of both of the originals, a guise of someone other than the originals, or simple misinterpretation on the part of humans. Lots of possibilities out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T14:04:17-08:00","id":47595,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the best way to handle it would be to decide which pantheon seems to be the &quot;home&quot; pantheon of the god (an entirely subjective thing) and use the psp for that pantheon for the particular god in all the &quot;guest&quot; pantheons as well. If a version is too different to resolve that way I would split the two into separate gods who get mistaken for each other (which could lead to some interesting humorous situations depending on what the gods involved think of their worshipers mixing them up like that). It may not be the most technically accurate way but it works for the story which is the important thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:09:20-08:00","id":47827,"title":"","content":"Well, this could be a problem, since some Japanese gods are Hindu gods, that moved through China, then eventually came to Japan. A number of the Fortunes for example fall under this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T05:20:16-08:00","id":48082,"title":"","content":"Interpretatio is going to be a thing in 2e. It's something all of the writers are keenly aware of, so we're taking that into account while designing the cosmology. As for PSPs, well. Those have changed a lot already. It's not fair or accurate to describe pantheon membership as a social club with fringe metaphysical benefits...but I wouldn't say it's fair to describe them as permanent mystical bloodlines anymore, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T06:40:15-08:00","id":48119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=48082#post48082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interpretatio is going to be a thing in 2e. It's something all of the writers are keenly aware of, so we're taking that into account while designing the cosmology. As for PSPs, well. Those have changed a lot already. It's not fair or accurate to describe pantheon membership as a social club with fringe metaphysical benefits...but I wouldn't say it's fair to describe them as permanent mystical bloodlines anymore, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! I got a dev response on one of my threads!<br /> <br /> This sounds very promising, Neall. It's good to know that this time around you guys are taking these things into account.<br /> <br /> So, would I be accurate in interpreting your statement here as meaning that a God can join another pantheon and just kind of have two separate identities? And that if he/she wants the new Pantheon's PSP, he/she may be able to gain it with some effort?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:34:19-08:00","id":48237,"title":"","content":"Close, but I'm really just stopping by to let you know that we're definitely considering interpretatio. That's probably the most definitive part of my statement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 01-13-2014, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:56:02-08:00","id":48264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=48237#post48237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Close, but I'm really just stopping by to let you know that we're definitely considering interpretatio. That's probably the most definitive part of my statement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. I'll just have fun wildly speculating for the time being.<br /> <br /> Thanks for telling us about interpretation, though. Seems like you guys are already putting a lot more thought into this edition than the previous edition, and as far as I'm concerned, that's all I could possibly ask of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T19:33:37-08:00","id":49476,"title":"","content":"I'm actually very happy to hear this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:02:03-08:00","id":49528,"title":"","content":"That is certainly interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1012-sorcerymon","name":"Sorcerymon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1012_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}